---
import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import { decisions } from '../data/decisions';

const homeCards = decisions.filter((d) => d.homeCard);
// Render only when the file exists.
const hasHeadshot = existsSync('public/img/headshot.webp');
const hasResume = existsSync('public/resume.pdf');
// ponytail: inner pages arrive in Phase 3. Cards, steps and the essay get their links then.
---

<Base
	title="Chander Maurya Kumbkarni"
	description="I worked on Google’s Pixel pricing through Smollan, then on a hotel’s costs in Dharamshala. I am looking for a Founder’s Office role that brings together everything I have learnt."
>
	<Hero />

	<section id="work" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="q-wrong">
		<p class="label">The Divine Hima · Dharamshala · 2026</p>
		<h2 id="q-wrong" class="t-question">Can he find the number that is <em>wrong</em>?</h2>
		<p class="lede">
			An independent engagement with a nine-room family hotel and its restaurant, from June 2026. No analytics
			team, no data warehouse.
		</p>
		<ol class="steps">
			<li>
				<span class="figure">5%</span>
				<p>One of three vendors printed prices without GST. The other two included it. Every comparison against that vendor was off by 5%.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="figure">₹139 to ₹113</span>
				<p>Rebuilt the cost of all 31 dishes from 17 vendor bills and 106 line items. The average cost per dish moved from ₹139 estimated to ₹113 actual. Modelled contribution up 28%.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="figure">73 to 31</span>
				<p>Cut the delivery menu from 73 items to 31 and repriced every survivor to a cost-derived target. Then checked every published price live against the plan. Exact match.</p>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="q-fix">
		<p class="label">Google via Smollan · Aug 2024 to Mar 2026</p>
		<h2 id="q-fix" class="t-question">Can he build the <em>fix</em>?</h2>
		<p class="lede">
			20 months at Smollan, a retail consultancy, supporting Google’s APAC and EMEA retail team.
		</p>
		<ol class="steps">
			<li>
				<span class="figure">2 to 4 hours</span>
				<p>Every week the analysis was assembled by hand: pull, clean, format.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="figure">1,000+ rows</span>
				<p>I built a Python pipeline that pulls 1,000+ rows of device and pricing data, adds AI-generated callouts and updates the dashboards on its own. It replaced the manual work.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="figure">32 people, 7 countries</span>
				<p>The dashboards were used by 32 people in 7 countries, including Mountain View, in the monthly Pixel pricing calls.</p>
			</li>
		</ol>
		<p class="note">Also: quarterly intelligence decks from three-plus years of panel data across 33 APAC and EMEA markets.</p>
	</section>

	<section id="decisions" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="q-judgement">
		<p class="label">Decisions</p>
		<h2 id="q-judgement" class="t-question">Does he have <em>judgement</em>?</h2>
		<p class="lede">Six times I went against the obvious move.</p>
		<ul class="cards">
			{homeCards.map((d) => (
				<li class="card">
					<p class="label">{d.source}</p>
					<h3>{d.title}</h3>
					<p class="why">{d.why}</p>
				</li>
			))}
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="q-unasked">
		<p class="label">Built on my own time</p>
		<h2 id="q-unasked" class="t-question">Does he ship <em>unasked</em>?</h2>
		<ul class="work">
			<li class="card">
				<p class="label">SuperYou Shelf Read · Sep 2026</p>
				<h3>A shelf audit nobody asked for.</h3>
				<p>Four findings from two evenings of public data.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="card">
				<p class="label">Finance system</p>
				<h3>A ledger that matches the card statements to the paisa.</h3>
				<p>Bank and card alerts become ledger entries on their own, and every statement is reconciled against them.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="card">
				<p class="label">Portfolio Monitor · demo mode</p>
				<h3>A monthly research note that writes and sends itself.</h3>
				<a class="poster glow" style="--glow: url(/img/portfolio-monitor.webp)" href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DzwqS973fmBsXSxNxthmFaoQc3jVDo8n/view">
					<img src="/img/portfolio-monitor.webp" width="1200" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Portfolio Monitor landing page: A research desk that runs itself, beside a demo-mode run log. Opens the two-minute walkthrough." />
				</a>
				<p class="links label">
					<a href="https://akamaurya.github.io/portfolio-monitor/">Landing page</a>
					<a href="https://github.com/akamaurya/portfolio-monitor">Code</a>
					<a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DzwqS973fmBsXSxNxthmFaoQc3jVDo8n/view">Walkthrough, demo mode</a>
				</p>
			</li>
			<li class="card loadbuddy">
				<p class="label">LoadBuddy</p>
				<h3>One screen. Green means push, orange means recover.</h3>
				<!-- A CSS recreation of the app's only screen. Hover or focus the card to switch phase. -->
				<div class="phone" aria-hidden="true">
					<div class="screen">
						<span class="phase load">LOAD</span>
						<span class="phase deload">DELOAD</span>
						<span class="next load">Next DELOAD is in 3 Days</span>
						<span class="next deload">Next LOAD is in 7 Days</span>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="links label">
					<a href="https://loadbuddy.vercel.app">Live app</a>
					<a href="https://github.com/akamaurya/LoadBuddy">Code</a>
				</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="q-truth">
		<p class="label">Gaps</p>
		<h2 id="q-truth" class="t-question">Will he tell me the <em>truth</em>?</h2>
		<div class="prose">
			<p><strong>What I have not done yet.</strong> I have not managed direct reports. I have coordinated teams without owning their performance. I have not run a paid ad account. I have worked full-time for 20 months.</p>
			<p><strong>How I use AI.</strong> I use AI agents heavily to do the building. I do not use them to decide what is worth building. This site was built that way: I specified it, tested it and shipped it.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="writing" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="q-range">
		<h2 id="q-range" class="label">Writing</h2>
		<ul class="writing">
			<li>
				<p class="label">Essay</p>
				<p class="essay">What 20 months of building pricing dashboards taught me: 7 lessons</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p class="label">LinkedIn article</p>
				<a class="essay" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/best-investment-research-kind-you-never-have-do-kumbkarni-g6o6c/">The best investment research is the kind you never have to do</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p class="label">LinkedIn article</p>
				<a class="essay" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/india-soft-power-evolving-battlefield-diplomacy-kumbkarni-e6txc/">India, Soft Power and the Evolving Battlefield of Diplomacy</a>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section id="contact" class="section wrap ask" aria-labelledby="q-ask">
		<div>
			<p class="label">The ask</p>
			<h2 id="q-ask" class="t-question">Based in Delhi. Available <em>immediately</em>.</h2>
			<p class="where">Bengaluru or Delhi preferred. Open to relocating anywhere in India or abroad.</p>
			<p class="actions">
				<!-- ponytail: Gmail compose works without a desktop mail app; the address beside it covers other mail clients -->
				<a class="button" href="https://mail.google.com/mail/?view=cm&amp;fs=1&amp;to=mkumbkarni@gmail.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Email me</a>
				<a class="label" href="mailto:mkumbkarni@gmail.com">mkumbkarni@gmail.com</a>
				<button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="mkumbkarni@gmail.com" aria-label="Copy email address" title="Copy email address" hidden><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="12" height="12" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10" /></svg></button>
				<a class="label" href="https://linkedin.com/in/mkumbkarni">LinkedIn</a>
				{hasResume && <a class="label" href="/resume.pdf">Resume</a>}
			</p>
		</div>
		{hasHeadshot && (
			<span class="headshot glow" style="--glow: url(/img/headshot.webp)">
				<img src="/img/headshot.webp" width="360" height="480" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Chander Maurya Kumbkarni" />
			</span>
		)}
	</section>
</Base>

<script>
	// Copy button: hidden in the markup, shown only when the clipboard API exists, so it never sits there dead.
	const copy = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]');
	if (copy && navigator.clipboard) {
		copy.hidden = false;
		const icon = copy.innerHTML;
		const tick = icon.replace(/<svg([^>]*)>[\s\S]*<\/svg>/, '<svg$1><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"></path></svg>');
		copy.addEventListener('click', async () => {
			try {
				await navigator.clipboard.writeText(copy.dataset.copy!);
				copy.innerHTML = tick;
				copy.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Copied');
			} catch {
				// Clipboard refused (permissions, embedded frames): select the address so a keyboard copy works.
				getSelection()?.selectAllChildren(copy.previousElementSibling!);
			}
			setTimeout(() => {
				copy.innerHTML = icon;
				copy.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Copy email address');
			}, 1500);
		});
	}
</script>

<script>
	// Scroll speed curve: wheel moves faster across section boundaries, slower while a section holds the screen.
	// ponytail: wheel only. Touch, keyboard and scrollbar scroll at native speed; add touch handling if phones need it too.
	const SLOW = 0.3; // at mid-section. Tune by feel.
	const FAST = 2; // with a boundary at mid-screen.
	const sections = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('main .section');
	if (!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
		addEventListener('wheel', (e) => {
			if (e.ctrlKey || Math.abs(e.deltaX) > Math.abs(e.deltaY)) return; // leave pinch-zoom and sideways swipes alone
			const mid = innerHeight / 2;
			const near = Math.min(...[...sections].map((s) => Math.abs(s.getBoundingClientRect().top - mid)));
			const t = Math.min(near / mid, 1);
			const k = FAST + (SLOW - FAST) * t * t * (3 - 2 * t); // smoothstep: fast at a boundary, easing to slow
			e.preventDefault();
			scrollBy(0, e.deltaY * (e.deltaMode === 1 ? 16 : 1) * k);
		}, { passive: false });
	}
</script>

<style>
	.section {
		padding-block: clamp(4rem, 12vh, 8rem);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}
	.section > .label { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
	h2 { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; max-width: 24ch; }
	h3 { font: 400 1.25rem/1.25 var(--serif); letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
	.lede { margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }

	/* Sections 2 and 3: three beats as a static stack. Scroll scenes enhance this in Phase 4. */
	.steps { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 2rem; }
	.steps li { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 1rem; }
	.steps p { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; }
	.figure {
		display: block;
		font: 500 clamp(1.75rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem)/1.1 var(--mono);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: var(--ink);
		text-wrap: balance;
	}
	.note { margin: 2rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-3); font-size: 0.94rem; }

	/* Cards */
	.cards, .work { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
	.card {
		background: var(--sheet);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1.5rem;
	}
	.card > .label { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
	.card p { margin: 0; }
	.why { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.94rem; }

	.poster { margin: 0.25rem 0 1rem; }
	.links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem; margin-top: 1rem !important; }
	.links a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
	.links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

	/* LoadBuddy screen, colours from the app */
	.phone {
		width: 140px;
		aspect-ratio: 9 / 19;
		margin: 0.5rem auto 0;
		border: 6px solid var(--ink);
		border-radius: 24px;
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.screen {
		height: 100%;
		display: grid;
		place-content: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		padding: 0.5rem;
		text-align: center;
		color: #fff;
		background: #009E4E;
		transition: background 0.35s ease;
	}
	.phase { font: 700 1.1rem/1 var(--sans); letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
	.next { font: 400 0.6rem/1.3 var(--mono); }
	.deload { display: none; }
	.loadbuddy:hover .screen, .loadbuddy:focus-within .screen { background: #C0651A; }
	.loadbuddy:hover .load, .loadbuddy:focus-within .load { display: none; }
	.loadbuddy:hover .deload, .loadbuddy:focus-within .deload { display: inline; }

	.prose p { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
	.prose strong { color: var(--ink); }

	.writing { list-style: none; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 1.75rem; }
	.writing .label { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
	.essay { display: block; font: 400 1.25rem/1.3 var(--serif); color: var(--ink); margin: 0; max-width: 40ch; }
	a.essay { text-decoration: none; }
	a.essay:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }

	.ask { display: grid; gap: 2.5rem; align-items: end; }
	.where { margin: 0; }
	.actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1rem 1.5rem; margin: 2rem 0 0; }
	.actions .label { color: var(--accent); }
	.actions a[href^="mailto"] { text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0.02em; }
	.copy { display: inline-grid; place-items: center; background: none; border: 0; padding: 0.25rem; margin-left: -0.75rem; color: var(--ink-3); cursor: pointer; }
	.copy:hover { color: var(--accent); }
	.button {
		text-shadow: none;
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.85rem 1.4rem;
		background: var(--accent);
		color: var(--paper);
		font: 700 0.8rem/1 var(--sans);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.14em;
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.button:hover { background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }
	.headshot { width: 140px; height: auto; }

	@media (min-width: 600px) {
		.cards, .work { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
	}
	@media (min-width: 768px) {
		.steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
		.ask { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; }
		.headshot { width: 180px; }
	}
	@media (min-width: 960px) {
		.cards { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
	}
</style>
